{
  "sn35.246:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.246 ",
  "sn35.246:0.2": "19. The Simile of the Vipers ",
  "sn35.246:0.3": "The Simile of the Harp ",
  "sn35.246:1.1": "“Mendicants, any monk or nun who has desire or greed or hate or delusion or aversion come up for sights known by the eye should shield their mind from them: ",
  "sn35.246:1.2": "‘This path is dangerous and perilous, thorny and tangled; it’s a wrong turn, a bad path, in poor condition. ",
  "sn35.246:1.3": "This path is frequented by untrue persons, not by true persons. ",
  "sn35.246:1.4": "It’s not worthy of you.’ ",
  "sn35.246:1.5": "The mind should be shielded from this when it comes to sights known by the eye. ",
  "sn35.246:1.6": "Any monk or nun who has desire or greed or hate or delusion or repulsion come up for sounds … smells … tastes … touches … ",
  "sn35.246:1.7": "ideas known by the mind should shield their mind against them: ",
  "sn35.246:1.8": "‘This path is dangerous and perilous, thorny and tangled; it’s a wrong turn, a bad path, a sorry state. ",
  "sn35.246:1.9": "This path is frequented by untrue persons, not by true persons. ",
  "sn35.246:1.10": "It’s not worthy of you.’ ",
  "sn35.246:1.11": "The mind should be shielded from this when it comes to ideas known by the mind. ",
  "sn35.246:2.1": "Suppose the crops have ripened, ",
  "sn35.246:2.2": "but the caretaker is negligent. If an ox fond of crops invades the crops they’d indulge themselves as much as they like. ",
  "sn35.246:2.3": "In the same